# armour/woman/tabard: the TABARD over-layer on the woman (STYLE_P2 28.3 over-layer; contracts 3c.1: `overlay tabard`, torso
# z 4 over the chest motif at z 3): the man's tabard re-cut to her torso: a 6-7 px cloth panel in the accent slot (tabardColor)
# from the collar to two rows below the hip, lit like A3's tunic (the lit plane left, the shadow side, the bust lit row 2
# and its under-shade row 3), side edges a step-0 line against the armour, belted, a solid lit hem; the device (5 px) on
# the chest is the `when device` region. The armour shows at the shoulders, on the arms and at the hips. Keys: rest idle
# run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L (her run and runl lift the belt a row; runl leans). FORGE-TORSO round 2 i1 (the
# area's tools/gen_tabw.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i2) a tabard covers the chest motif, so it wears the motif as a heraldic charge (`when motif-<v>`,
# the block at the end): bars, a V, a saltire, a sun, a chief, a pale, a roundel.
# (INTEGRATE silhouettes i2) facing R and L the panel ends at her plate's hem (two rows shorter, the solid lit hem kept):
# hanging two rows below the hip it was narrower than her stride (B11 HIPLINE 3 px on the walk).
use person
body woman
role overlay tabard
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 4
legend D device 2
legend Q device 3
legend H device 1

